{"description":"Trampoline Hall is this:\nThree people give lectures on topics on which they are not professionally expert, followed by Q&A.\n\nShows happen every month in Toronto and a few times a year in San Francisco. It usually sells out very quickly.\n\nRead More About The Show\n\n\"We love it!\" - The Village Voice\n“Eccentricity and do-it-yourself inventiveness.” - The New Yorker\n\n\nThe next one is on Monday, October 5th at The Garrison.\nDoors open at 7:00pm and the show starts at 7:30pm sharp.\nTickets will be available online (here) starting on Thursday, October 1st at 10am ET.\nAll speakers this month chosen by Charles Yao & Emily M. Keeler\nLectures by...\nRebecca Tucker - \"BUGS\"\nVanya Garraway - \"NAPS\"\nMeredith Cheesbrough - \"MOMS\"\nSet design by... Lena Rubisova\n\nTrampoline Hall was created by Sheila Heti and is hosted by Misha Glouberman. Misha also runs Toronto Event Generator, which fosters the creation of cool events in Toronto with micro-grants and other support, and also runs a great newsletter of cool smart weird events in Toronto.\nIf tickets are sold out, you can join the waitlist here and we'll let you know if tickets free up","organizer":"Trampoline Hall"}